      "kind": "issue",
      "title": "Duplicate Spec-of-algebra-map Over-morphisms: `AlgebraicGeometry.overSpecMap` vs `AlgebraicGeometry.Over.overSpecMap`",
      "latest": "Janitor re-measurement (2026-07-31, 15 days after filing): STILL LIVE, and both sides have grown a lot of consumers, so this is now a rename with a real blast radius rather than a cheap fix.\n\n- `AlgebraicGeometry.Over.overSpecMap` (`Picard/RelPicAlgebra.lean:44`, from an `A →ₐ[k] B`): **77** files reference it.\n- `AlgebraicGeometry.overSpecMap` (`Cohomology/RelativeSectionsLinear.lean:147`, from a plain algebra map): **27** files. The enclosing `section CurveMap` adds nothing to the name, so the two really do sit in one namespace differing only by the `Over.` prefix.\n\nNot a janitor fix: picking which survives and repairing ~100 call sites is a lane decision on a shared API. Leaving open with the numbers attached so whoever takes it can price it."
